{"id":"6ea335c4-3ad9-4d2a-ac47-ece07f2f002f","createdAt":"2026-10-26T13:14:41.404Z","batchId":"profile_claude-sonnet-5-5_low","approach":"html","modelId":"claude-sonnet-5-5","settings":{"effort":"low"},"presetId":"profile","prompt":"A user profile card with avatar, name, role, short bio, a few stats and a follow button.","system":"Return only the body content of an HTML page: no doctype, <html>, <head> or <body> tags, no markdown, no code fences, no prose. The page shell below is already loaded, so build with its classes and chart helper. Inline <script> is allowed for interactivity (tabs, toggles, filters); no external requests. Add a small <style> block only for what the classes cannot express, or when the request asks for a different look, colours, fonts or layout: then follow the request.\nPAGE SHELL (already loaded; do not restate it):\n- A stylesheet with these classes. Use them instead of writing CSS:\n  layout: page (centered column), stack, row, between, center, gap-sm, gap-lg, grid + cols-2|cols-3|cols-4 (responsive)\n  surfaces: card, card-title, card-desc, alert, alert-destructive, hr\n  text: h1-h4 (styled), lead, muted, small, up, down (trend colours)\n  controls: btn, btn-secondary|btn-outline|btn-ghost|btn-destructive, btn-sm|btn-lg, btn-block; label wraps input/select/textarea; label.check wraps a checkbox or radio\n  data: table (styled; td.num for numbers), badge, badge-secondary|badge-outline|badge-destructive, stat-label, stat-value, progress (inner div with style=\"width:NN%\"), avatar\n- Charts: <div data-chart='{\"type\":\"bar|line|area|pie\",\"title\":\"…\",\"data\":[{\"label\":\"W1\",\"value\":120}]}'></div> renders an SVG chart (single series, pie gets a legend). Do not draw charts yourself.\n- Light and dark mode are handled by the stylesheet.\n\nDESIGN BRIEF (applies to every UI you produce):\n- Build a complete, realistic screen, not a skeleton: a clear title and intro, grouped sections, and enough detail that it could ship.\n- Cover exactly what the request names, with no extra pages or marketing sections.\n- Use the supplied DATA in full: every field is there to be shown. Derive useful extras from it (shares, totals, deltas, rankings) instead of inventing unrelated numbers.\n- Where it fits, add status badges, trend/change figures, secondary actions, helper text, and sensible empty or edge-case copy.\n- Establish hierarchy with headings, size and weight; group related items; keep spacing and alignment consistent.\n- Make charts readable: a title, labelled axes or values, and a legend for pie charts.\n- Never use lorem ipsum or placeholder names like \"Item 1\".","systemHash":"0c16911c9564c3db3ada7a622931ee6ffc820ebf9a373996782a9f1f0fc3c98c","systemOverridden":false,"strictOutput":false,"rawOutput":"<style>\n.pc-wrap{max-width:440px;margin:0 auto}\n.pc-avatar{width:84px;height:84px;font-size:28px}\n.pc-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);text-align:center;gap:8px}\n.pc-stats div{padding:10px 4px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(127,127,127,.08)}\n</style>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <div class=\"pc-wrap stack gap-lg\">\n    <div>\n      <h1 class=\"h2\">Profile</h1>\n      <p class=\"muted\">Preview of how a member appears to the community.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card stack\">\n      <div class=\"row gap-lg\">\n        <div class=\"avatar pc-avatar center\">MR</div>\n        <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n          <div>\n            <h2 class=\"h3\" style=\"margin:0\">Maya Rodriguez</h2>\n            <span class=\"muted small\">@mayarodriguez · Lisbon, Portugal</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"row gap-sm\">\n            <span class=\"badge\">Staff Product Designer</span>\n            <span class=\"badge badge-outline\">Pro</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <p>Designing calm, accessible tools for teams that ship. Previously at Figma and Spotify. I write about design systems, mentor early-career designers, and run a monthly critique circle.</p>\n      <div class=\"pc-stats\">\n        <div><div class=\"stat-value\" id=\"followers\">12.4k</div><div class=\"stat-label\">Followers</div></div>\n        <div><div class=\"stat-value\">386</div><div class=\"stat-label\">Following</div></div>\n        <div><div class=\"stat-value\">142</div><div class=\"stat-label\">Posts</div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"row gap-sm\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-block\" id=\"followBtn\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Follow</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-outline\">Message</button>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"muted small\" id=\"note\" style=\"margin:0\">Follow Maya to see new posts in your feed.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var b=document.getElementById('followBtn'),f=document.getElementById('followers'),n=document.getElementById('note'),on=false;\n  b.addEventListener('click',function(){\n    on=!on;\n    b.textContent=on?'Following':'Follow';\n    b.classList.toggle('btn-secondary',on);\n    b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',on);\n    f.textContent=on?'12.4k+':'12.4k';\n    n.textContent=on?'You will see Maya\\u2019s new posts in your feed.':'Follow Maya to see new posts in your feed.';\n  });\n})();\n</script>","deltas":[[795,"<style"],[1066,">\n.p"],[1069,"c-"],[1069,"wrap{max-width:"],[1069,"440px;margin:0 "],[1069,"auto}\n.pc-"],[1069,"av"],[1069,"atar{width:84"],[1097,"px;height:84px;font"],[1133,"-size:28"],[1171,"px}"],[1209,"\n.pc-st"],[1241,"ats{display:gr"],[1383,"id;grid-template-colum"],[1383,"ns:repeat(3,"],[1383,"1fr);text"],[1387,"-align:center;gap:"],[1423,"8px}\n.pc-"],[1460,"stats div{padding:10"],[1492,"px 4"],[1530,"px;border-radius:8"],[1569,"px;"],[1616,"background:r"],[1637,"gba(127"],[1673,",127,127,.08)"],[1711,"}\n</style>\n<div"],[1747," class=\"page\">"],[1777,"\n  "],[1822,"<div class=\"pc-w"],[1851,"rap st"],[1886,"ack g"],[1924,"ap-lg\">\n    <"],[1959,"div>"],[1993,"\n      <h1 class=\""],[2027,"h2"],[2065,"\">"],[2098,"Profile<